# p_4a7e — The Daily Commuter: Hana Out Every Weekday 8 to 17:30

Hana works in an office in town, five days a week, leaving at roughly 8:00 and returning at 17:30. She is not a hybrid worker: there is no Tuesday or Thursday on which she sits at desk_b1. Every single weekday she takes her laptop, jacket, keys, handbag, pen, scarf, sunglasses, wallet, phone, charger, shoes, and water bottle out the door with her. None of these items are in the house between 8:00 and 17:30 on a weekday. By 18:30 she is home and has hung her jacket and scarf on the entry hook, set her keys and wallet on the entry table, placed her shoes on the shoe rack, put her laptop and charger at desk_b1, set her phone on the nightstand, and left her water bottle at the kitchen sink or counter.

This document directly contradicts p_b7c2 (the hybrid model that puts Hana at desk_b1 on Tuesdays) and p_f5a0 (the no-laptop-travel model). The per-object evidence is unambiguous: on the two sighted weekdays, every look at entry_hook_e1, entry_table_e1, desk_b1, and shoe_rack_e1 during 9–17 h found nothing for Hana's personal items. On Wednesday morning (day 1), Hana was absent from the kitchen at both 8:00 and 10:00, while Priya was present — consistent with a full commuter who has already left.

What would refute this document: a sighting of Hana's laptop, jacket, or keys anywhere in the house during weekday 9–17 h, or a look at the entry hook/table during that window that finds them.

