# p_8c3d — Evening Kitchen: Cook at Counter, Eat at Table, Wash at Sink

The weekday evening kitchen follows a three-act sequence. Act one (17:30–19:00): Hana and Priya cook dinner at the counter. The pan, pot, cutting board, knife, and spatula are all on counter_k1; the recipe book may be propped up nearby. Act two (19:00–20:00): they eat at the kitchen table. Glasses, mugs, plates, and the water bottle are all at kitchen_table_k1. The snack bowl, if brought out for the meal, is also at the table. Act three (20:00–21:00): washing up. The cutting board, knife, pan, and pot move to sink_k1 to be rinsed. The snack bowl goes to sink_k1. Plates return to cupboard_k1. Glasses and mugs are put away or left at the table.

This document explains the mixture's worst-object errors at 20:00 on day 0 (Tuesday): the cutting board and knife were at sink_k1 (not ON_PERSON, not at counter), the snack bowl was at sink_k1 (not coffee_table_l1), the glasses and mugs were at kitchen_table_k1 (not sink_k1), the water bottle was at kitchen_table_k1 (not ON_PERSON), and the pot was at counter_k1 (left over from cooking, not yet washed). It also corrects the tendency of other documents to put the snack bowl at coffee_table_l1 during the evening — that is the TV-snack location, not the dinner location.

